'''Sirro Argonne''' was a [[human]] [[Gender|male]] [[scientist]] who served in the [[Galactic Republic]]'s [[Ministry of Science (Galactic Republic)|Ministry of Science]] before becoming an operations specialist in the [[Galactic Empire]]'s [[Tarkin Initiative]]. As part of a [[Kyber crystal research team|team]] researching [[kyber crystal]]s under scientist [[Galen Walton Erso|Galen Erso]], Argonne worked in captivity in a [[Eadu Energy Conversion Laboratory|laboratory]] on the [[planet]] [[Eadu]], where he saw to the needs of his colleagues and [[Administrator|administered]] the facility.

By [[1 BBY]], the team's work had produced a functioning [[Mk I Superlaser|superlaser]] for the Empire's [[DS-1 Orbital Battle Station|Death Star]] [[superweapon]]; however, after Erso sent a message to the [[Alliance to Restore the Republic]] about the [[weapon]], [[Director]] [[Orson Callan Krennic|Orson Krennic]] arrived on Eadu to punish whichever team member had betrayed the Empire. Although Erso admitted that he was the [[Treason|traitor]] to try and save Argonne and his colleagues from [[Death penalty|execution]], Krennic had the operations specialist [[Death|killed]] along with the rest of the team anyway.

==Biography==
===Lab admin===
[[File:Eadu_Scientific_research_base.png|thumb|right|300px|Sirro Argonne administered a secret laboratory on Eadu.]]
Sirro Argonne was a [[human]]<ref name="ROUVG" /> [[Gender|male]] [[engineer]]<ref name="RO" /> and [[scientist]] who served as a member of the [[Galactic Republic]]'s [[Ministry of Science (Galactic Republic)|Ministry of Science]]. After the Republic was [[Proclamation of the New Order|replaced]] by the [[Galactic Empire]]<ref name="ROUVG" /> in [[19 BBY]],<ref name="Timelines">''[[Star Wars: Timelines]]''</ref> he became an operations specialist in the [[Tarkin Initiative]], which was led by [[Director]] [[Orson Callan Krennic|Orson Krennic]] and was responsible for the creation of the [[DS-1 Orbital Battle Station|Death Star]] [[superweapon]]. Argonne became part of a [[Kyber crystal research team|team]] of six scientists tasked with finding out how to fuse the [[kyber crystal]]s used by the [[Death Star]]'s [[Mk I Superlaser|superlaser]] into larger forms and how to create and redirect a controlled chain reaction of the [[crystal]]s.<ref name="ROUVG" />

The records for each member of the team were deleted from public databases once their work began,<ref name="RebelDossier">''[[Star Wars: Rogue One: Rebel Dossier]]''</ref> and the group was held captive in a [[Eadu Energy Conversion Laboratory|secret laboratory]] on the [[planet]] [[Eadu]].<ref name="ROUVG" /> Argonne was a civil servant<ref name="Geektionary">''[[Star Wars: Geektionary: The Galaxy from A - Z]]''</ref> who [[Administrator|administered]] the facility<ref name="ROUVG" /> and managed the scientists, taking care of their wellbeing<ref name="Geektionary" /> and seeing that their needs were met. This included both material requirements<ref name="ROUVG" /> in the [[laboratory]]<ref name="Geektionary" /> and personal requirements<ref name="ROUVG" /> in their [[Standard day|day]]-to-day lives.<ref name="Geektionary" />

===Progress===
{{Quote|What is it you want?''"<br />"''The work has stalled. I need you to come back.|Galen Erso and Orson Krennic discuss the work of the kyber crystal research team|audio=Galen-Krennic-Stalled-RO.flac|<ref name="RO" />}}
[[File:SirroGalen-RO.png|thumb|left|300px|Argonne (left) worked as part of the kyber crystal research team led by Galen Erso on Eadu.]]
By [[13 BBY]],<ref name="ErsoDate">''[[Star Wars: Timelines]]'' dates [[Galen Walton Erso]]'s [[Capture of Galen Erso|capture]] on [[Lah'mu]] to [[13 BBY]].</ref> the group's work had stalled,<ref name="RO" /> leaving the project [[Standard year|years]] behind schedule,<ref name="Rise">''[[Star Wars: The Rise and Fall of the Galactic Empire]]''</ref> and so Krennic [[Capture of Galen Erso|abducted]] [[Galen Walton Erso|Galen Erso]], a [[Crystallography|crystallographer]] who had previously worked with Krennic, and brought him to Eadu as a reluctant new leader for the team.<ref name="RO" /> Thanks to Erso's extraordinary intellect, the group of scientist's progress was revitalized, causing them to successfully complete their given tasks<ref name="Novel">[[Rogue One: A Star Wars Story (novelization)|''Rogue One: A Star Wars Story'' novelization]]</ref> by [[1 BBY]],<ref name="Date" /> allowing the Death Star to be equipped with a functional [[weapon]].<ref name="RO" />

In total, the team had remained in seclusion on the planet for nearly twenty years to achieve this.<ref name="ROUVG" /> After the weapon was complete, Erso secretly had the [[pilot]] [[Bodhi Rook]] deliver a message to the rebellious [[partisans]]' leader, [[Saw Gerrera]], on the [[moon]] [[Jedha]], asking him to bring information of a [[Thermal exhaust port|structural weakness]] that Erso had built into the Death Star to the [[Alliance to Restore the Republic]].<ref name="RO" />

===Execution===
{{Quote|Gentlemen. One of you has betrayed the Empire. One of you conspired with a pilot to send messages to the Rebellion. I urge that traitor to step forward.|Krennic confronts Argonne and his colleagues|audio=KrennicScientistsEadu.flac|<ref name="RO" />}}
[[File:EaduScientists.png|thumb|right|300px|Orson Krennic accused the kyber crystal research team of treachery.]]
Once Krennic was informed by [[Grand Moff]] [[Wilhuff Tarkin]] that information had leaked from the laboratory, he personally traveled to Eadu to find the source of the betrayal.<ref name="RO" /> Argonne and the other scientists were informed of the impending arrival of Krennic's [[ST-149|shuttle]],<ref name="RO 3">[[Rogue One Adaptation 3|''Rogue One Adaptation'' 3]]</ref> and the director ordered Erso to gather the weapon's six chief engineers<ref name="Birth">{{EncyclopediaCite|The Birth of the Rebellion}}</ref> on the facility's landing pad. Prior to the [[shuttle]]'s arrival, Argonne, Erso, and the five other team members followed [[stormtrooper]]s out onto the platform and huddled to speak in the [[Water|rain]],<ref name="RO" /> sodden, haggard, and displeased to be outside so late.<ref name="Novel" />

Although the group was used to unannounced inspections,<ref name="HC49">{{HelmetCollectionCite|49|Weapons & Uniforms}}</ref> as the Empire conducted inspections on the team regularly,<ref name="ROUVG" /> the [[Krennic's guard squadron|squad]] of [[death trooper]]s that accompanied Krennic as he disembarked<ref name="RO" /> represented a foreboding<ref name="HC49" /> change in their fates.<ref name="ROUVG" /> The director looked over the gathered scientists and recalled each of their names, studying their postures and noting no defiance. With the miserable team stood in a loose, indecorous cluster while corralled by the stormtroopers,<ref name="Novel" /> Erso approached Krennic alone. After informing the scientist that that the Death Star was complete, Krennic ordered him to gather his team for an announcement. Argonne and the others<ref name="RO" /> stepped forward timidly,<ref name="RO AD">''[[Rogue One: A Star Wars Story]]'' {{AD|Disney+}}</ref> drifting in a herd-like fashion across the platform and then huddling together as though to ward off the cold and their collective dread<ref name="Novel" /> as Erso returned to Krennic's side. The director then declared that one of the scientists was a [[Treason|traitor]] who had colluded with the rebels and urged the individual to step forward. Erso's team gasped and murmured among themselves, but no one stepped forward as Krennic's death [[trooper]]s moved into position alongside the director.<ref name="RO" /> 

[[File:SirroDeath-RO.png|thumb|left|300px|Despite his innocence, Argonne was executed on the orders of Krennic.]]
With no confession, the director explained that the betrayal would be considered a group effort and ordered the troopers to take aim. The scientists cried out in protest before Erso stepped in front of them and admitted that he was the traitor, asking Krennic to spare his team. The director beckoned Erso away from the others,<ref name="RO" /> who were all relieved but too shocked and unsure of the situation to offer their savior thanks. Despising the group,<ref name="Junior">''[[Star Wars: Rogue One: A Junior Novel]]''</ref> Krennic had his troopers open fire, [[Death penalty|killing]] Argonne and the others where they stood. Erso was [[Death|killed]] soon after when the Alliance [[Mission to Eadu|bombed]] the laboratory, which forced Krennic to flee.<ref name="RO" /> In [[35 ABY]],<ref name="RiseDate">{{RiseAndFallDate}}</ref> the [[historian]] [[Beaumont Kin]] negatively compared the team that Argonne was part of to Erso in<ref name="Rise" /> his<ref name="TROSVD">''[[Star Wars: The Rise of Skywalker: The Visual Dictionary]]''</ref> [[book]] ''[[The Rise and Fall of the Galactic Empire]]''.<ref name="Rise" />

==Personality and traits==
{{Quote|In Erso's absence Krennic was forced to try and persevere with his other captive scientists, none of whom possessed the raw intellect of the man he had lost.|Beaumont Kin, ''The Rise and Fall of the Galactic Empire''|<ref name="Rise" />}}
Arogonne was a scientific genius<ref name="ROUVG" /> who showed care toward the project on Eadu, although this did not save him from execution,<ref name="Geektionary" /> with Krennic considering the scientist and his colleagues sniveling weaklings.<ref name="Junior" /> He had [[Color|blue]] [[eye]]s, light skin, and [[hair]] that was gray<ref name="ROUVG" /> by the [[time]] of his death.<ref name="RO" /> By that point, Argonne was also frail and unused to being outdoors due to his time working in the laboratories on Eadu.<ref name="Junior" /> In his book, Kin claimed that neither Arrgone or any of Krennic's other captive scientists possessed Erso's "raw intellect."<ref name="Rise" /> 

==Equipment==
[[File:TarkinInitiative.svg|thumb|right|200px|Argonne's uniform bore the Tarkin Initiative's emblem.]]
While on Eadu, Argonne wore [[Jumpsuit|antiseptic coveralls]] to prevent lab contamination and carried a pair of [[code cylinder]]s that granted him access to the high security laboratories. Argonne's [[Clothing|coveralls]] were marked with the [[Imperial crest|insignia]] of both the Empire and the Tarkin Initiative,<ref name="ROUVG" /> the latter of which was inspired by a fractured kyber crystal.<ref name="AEYNTK">''[[Star Wars: Absolutely Everything You Need to Know, Updated and Expanded]]''</ref> The coveralls also bore blue sections across the neck and shoulders that changed color as a warning when revealed to high levels of [[radiation]]. The [[Antiseptic coveralls|outfit's]] [[boot]]s were grounded to prevent potentially dangerous static discharges occurring in the labs.<ref name="ROUVG" />

==Behind the scenes==
{{Quote|For the Visual Guide, gave a bunch of these scientists names that were basically phonemes made up of Los Alamos scientists' names chopped up, tossed into a blender and stuck together again.|Pablo Hidalgo|<ref name="Twitter">{{Twitter|username=pabl0hidalgo|url=status/1727942382644256970|name=[[Pablo Hidalgo]]|date=2023-11-24|quote=For the Visual Guide, gave a bunch of these scientists names that were basically phonemes made up of Los Alamos scientists' names chopped up, tossed into a blender and stuck together again.|archivefile=File:PabloLosAlamosTweet.png}}</ref>}}
[[File:EaduScientistsConcept.jpg|thumb|right|300px|Jon McCoy's concept artwork of the Eadu scientists' deaths for ''Rogue One: A Star Wars Story''.]]
Sirro Argonne first appeared in the [[Star Wars Anthology Series|Anthology Series]] film, ''[[Rogue One: A Star Wars Story]]'',<ref name="RO" /> as well as in its [[Rogue One: A Star Wars Story (novelization)|adult]]<ref name="Novel" /> and [[Star Wars: Rogue One: A Junior Novel|junior novelizations]],<ref name="Junior" /> which released the same day as the film on [[December 16]], [[2016]].<ref name="SW.com">{{SW|url=news/rebel-reading-rogue-one-books|text=Rebel Reading: A Guide to ''Rogue One'' Books|author=[[James Floyd|Floyd, James]]|date=2016-12-14}}</ref> The character was portrayed by [[Richard Franklin]] and identified only as "Engineer" in the credits.<ref name="RO" /> Prior to the film's release, the character was revealed in the second trailer for the film, which released on [[October 13]], 2016.<ref name="Trailer">{{SWYouTube|sC9abcLLQpI|Rogue One: A Star Wars Story Trailer #2 (Official)|sw_url=video/rogue-one-a-star-wars-story-trailer-2}}</ref>

Argonne was first identified in ''[[Star Wars: Rogue One: The Ultimate Visual Guide]]'', a reference book written by [[Pablo Hidalgo]]<ref name="ROUVG" /> released on the same day as the film.<ref name="SW.com" /> Hidalgo created several of the scientists' names by combining elements from the names of the real-life scientists associated with the [[Wikipedia:Los Alamos National Laboratory|Los Alamos National Laboratory]].<ref name="Twitter" /> For ''Rogue One'', concept artwork of the scientists' death scene was created by artist [[Jon McCoy]].<ref name="Artbook">''[[The Art of Rogue One: A Star Wars Story]]''</ref> Argonne was pictured in a card made as a promo for the ''[[Secrets of Power]]'' set of the [[Fantasy Flight Games]] [[Star Wars: Unlimited|''Star Wars'': Unlimited]] card game<ref name="SWU">{{SWU|set=Secrets of Power|cardname=Galen Erso|subtitle=You'll Never Win|type=PQ Participation|link=4229452447}}</ref> that was released on [[November 7]], [[2025]].<ref name="SSU">{{UnlimitedWeb|url=products/set-6-secrets-of-power|text=Set 6 Secrets of Power}}</ref> The card's artwork was drawn by [[Axel Hutt]] in [[2024]].<ref name="Axel">{{Bluesky|smirt.bsky.social|post/3mdlzt3vl522j|[[Axel Hutt]]|date=2026-01-29|quote="Galen Erso" for Star Wars Unlimited. I drew that in 2024.
Also, abolish ICE.|archiveurl=https://ghostarchive.org/archive/CXVcW}}</ref>

